From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pogo-bash <pogo-bash@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:16:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb: canvas and SVG parity: isPointInStroke, text drawing
 style attributes, ink-box measureText, WebP serialization, SVG images without
 a compositor, SVG character positions

isPointInStroke() hit-tests the stroke outline (width, caps, joins, miter
limit, dashes) through Skia's FillPathWithPaint. wordSpacing, fontKerning,
fontStretch, fontVariantCaps, textRendering and lang exist with the spec's
defaults and setter rules (stored; the shaper does not apply them yet).
measureText's actualBoundingBox* are the glyphs' ink box relative to the
textAlign point, not the font's ascent and descent. toDataURL/toBlob
serialize image/webp (lossless). An embedder without a compositor host can
install an in-process rasterizer for SVG image frames, so drawImage of an
SVG <img> draws. getStartPositionOfChar was a stub answering (0, 0); it and
the new getEndPositionOfChar, getRotationOfChar and getCharNumAtPosition
read the glyph cells layout commits, which now carry their baseline.
